## Summary

Fixes the remaining live catalog-refresh failure where Playwright scrolls the ChatGPT conversation sidebar while retrying an inference-control click.

## Live evidence

The failing browser trace shows a real ChatGPT history link intercepting the click:

`<a data-sidebar-item="true" aria-label="Modelo de conversación" href="/c/...">…</a>`

Playwright then retries the action and scrolls the page/sidebar while trying to make the target clickable.

## Fix

- explicitly classify `data-sidebar-item` and `/c/...` links as chat-history/sidebar surfaces;
- route picker, model option, effort option, and catalog-discovery clicks through one guarded click path;
- hit-test the intended target before clicking with `elementFromPoint()`;
- refuse targets outside the current viewport instead of allowing Playwright auto-scroll;
- refuse clicks when the hit point resolves to another element or any sidebar/history surface;
- emit target/hit/sidebar diagnostics in the resulting `AdapterMismatch`;
- use viewport-coordinate mouse clicks only after the guard proves the target is directly clickable.

## Regression coverage

Adds a controlled Chromium fixture reproducing the exact `data-sidebar-item="true"`, `aria-label="Modelo de conversación"`, `/c/...` interceptor. The test requires the adapter to fail closed before the picker receives any click. A second regression verifies weak picker candidates nested inside `data-sidebar-item` are rejected.

## Release

Bumps Cofer U Pass and the ChatGPT adapter to 1.2.4. `rule_version` remains 1.2.0 because declarative rules did not change.

## Validation

The repository still has no GitHub Actions workflow, and this execution environment cannot access the repository checkout/Playwright Chromium to execute the suite. The complete diff is being code-reviewed before merge; the supervised live refresh remains the final provider-UI acceptance gate.

